  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nCompletes open question 2 of [#2593](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2593) (`research/triadic-query-pair`, kernel-3 specialization of [#840](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/840)): for every positive odd kernel `q`, the same three-query fusion at `a=\u00b1q\u00b72^j` attains the typed invoice below on every **odd modulus coprime to `q`**. Even moduli and odd moduli sharing a prime with `q` are excluded. Typed costs do **not** improve over the dyadic (`q=1`) case.\n\n```text\nx <- h^-a x\nx ^= y\nx <- h^(2a) x\nx ^= y\nx <- h^-a x\n```\n\n| Complete cost item | Separate pair | Fused odd-kernel pair |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Ordinary recursive children | 4 | 3 |\n| Ordered affine events | 24 | 18 |\n| Aligned XOR scans | 4 | 2 |\n| Extra full private rows | 0 | 0 |\n\nCertificate kernels: `{1,3,5,7,9,15}` (dyadic recovery, triadic cross-check, and primary new `{5,7,9,15}`). Pattern: admitted \u21d4 odd and `gcd(modulus,q)=1`.\n\n**Research construction / recursive interface; no new kappa.** Leave-alone through [#2686](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2686) (including [#2677](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2677), [#2643](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2643), [#2593](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2593)) was not reopened.\n\n## Result\n\nPackage: `research/odd-kernel-query-pair/`.\nTip: `c319093b5b96211e89165f4ad9dd0d20d5039414`.\n\nExact invoice **children 4\u21923; affine 24\u219218; XOR 4\u21922** uniformly across certified odd kernels; no typed gain over dyadic.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/odd-kernel-query-pair/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/odd-kernel-query-pair/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -B research/odd-kernel-query-pair/independent.py\npython3.12 -I -B research/odd-kernel-query-pair/test_package.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/odd-kernel-query-pair\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_ODD_KERNEL_QUERY_PAIR kernels=[1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 15] primary_new=[5, 7, 9, 15] children=4->3 affine=24->18 xor=4->2 no_typed_gain_over_dyadic ... no_new_kappa\nPASS_INDEPENDENT_ODD_KERNEL_QUERY_PAIR kernels=[1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 15] ... no_new_kappa\nPASS_ODD_KERNEL_QUERY_PAIR_PACKAGE_TESTS groups=6\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/odd-kernel-query-pair outcome=completed\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Admission uses `need()`; `-O` also passes.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest priors: [#840](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/840) dyadic; [#2593](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2593) kernel-3 (OQ2). Freestanding generalization; does not edit those packages. No competing open PR on this multi-kernel pattern at refresh.\n\nCredit Wentao Li / PR840 / #2593 lineage. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
